    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who registers our highest efficiency score at 83.29. Facing Bibee, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 16% park factor boost and a favorable SP skill matchup, with the added benefit of a slow opposing delivery that keeps his stolen base ceiling viable despite a league-average catcher. **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) serve as high-floor engines; **Jackson Merrill** is positioned to exploit a weak 5.59 xERA matchup against Cornelio, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizes on a stellar 17% SP skill adjustment and advantageous platoon dynamics. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains a staple in the heart of the order, providing a high-ceiling 66.54 score buoyed by a significant park advantage in his matchup against Perkins.\n\nThe bench decision process was tightest at the corner spots, where **Tommy White** (52.17) narrowly missed the final slot. While **Tommy White** benefits from favorable park conditions, he ultimately lost out to the superior platoon adjustments and higher raw projections of **Coby Mayo** (61.85) and **Miguel Vargas** (61.34). **Miguel Vargas** is particularly notable today, as his 0.385 xwOBA trend suggests he is currently undervalued by baseline projections, prompting his start over more traditional power options. We are also closely monitoring the utility slots; **Liam Hicks** and **Drake Baldwin** both hover near the 60.00 threshold, but we are keeping them active to protect against volatility in the middle of our order.\n\nInvestors should remain cautious regarding the volume of right-handed hitters facing RHP today, though the \"Dynamic Platoon\" adjustments are largely insulating our production against these matchups. We have no major weather threats, but the reliance on **Luis Lara** (48.58) as our lone OF2 outlier is a strategic risk we are carrying to maximize our positional versatility. Given the ongoing absences of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jordan Westburg** on the IL, our current depth is being pushed to its limit, making every fractional point from **Henry Bolte** (58.98) and **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) critical as we navigate the scarcity of the stolen base category.",
